From 8fec8b3c5ed76d88c1c9e1a0f75a0e77076f0eb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:17:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/32] Direct3D layer, step 3: textures

- textures bound per stage: NV2A format word (swizzled uncompressed formats, DXT1/3/5), address,
  filters, max LOD; texture shader stages set to 2D projective
- mip levels packed back to back as the NV2A finds them (the step-1 layout padded each level)
- uncompressed power-of-two textures keep a linear copy for LockRect and are swizzled into the
  GPU copy before their next draw when dirty (unlocks, surface unlocks, UpdateTexture); DXT
  textures are not swizzled on the NV2A and keep a single copy
- xbox_d3d8_combiners.cpp: the swizzle, and Direct3D texture-stage operations translated to
  register combiners (select, modulate x1/2/4, add, signed add, subtract, smooth add, the blend
  and modulate-add families, dot product), specular added by the final combiner
- not yet: non-power-of-two textures, coordinate generation and texture matrices (logged once)
